     "text": "Architecture decision record Keep the advisor tooling in this repo The shoulder-advisor port stays beside the blog it reviews. What that costs, how the cost is kept small, and what would reopen the question. We will keep the advisor tooling (the post ingesters, the advisor CLI, the corpus layout and the leak check) in this repo, because its review pipeline works on this blog's own pages, the leak check has to stay here whichever way we go, and moving would save about 18 MB of install and no CI job at the price of a second repo. It also keeps the consolidation the owner chose when the port began. The cost is bounded by five conditions below, and seven triggers reopen the question."
